HST Office: a toolbar's delayed controller update never runs while the toolbar removes its controllers.

ToolBarManager updates its controllers from a 50 ms timer (AsyncUpdateControllersHdl ->
UpdateControllers -> XUpdatable::update). RemoveControllers() disposes the controllers one by one, and
dispose() deliberately stops that timer only at its end. A controller's dispose() can release the
SolarMutex: on Windows a window destroyed by a thread other than the main thread is handed to the main
thread with SendMessage, and the SolarMutex is released while waiting (WinSalInstance::SendWndMessage_impl).
That is the case for a document loaded or closed over the UNO bridge (an automation client): the toolbars
of the old view are destroyed on the bridge's request thread. The main thread can then run the pending
timer and update a controller that is half disposed.

Windows smoke of 1.0.0 crashed this way: a request thread in Desktop::loadComponentFromURL was in
LayoutManager::destroyElement -> ToolBarManager::dispose -> RemoveControllers -> the style box
controller's disposing() -> the box window's dispose, waiting for the SolarMutex, while the main thread
ran the timer and the style box controller filled its box: m_xVclBox already moved out, the box's
weld::ComboBox released, read of address 0 in FillStyleBox (earlier builds: ReBind on a released family
listener).

AsyncUpdateControllersHdl now returns while RemoveControllers() runs. The toolbar is then being refilled
(FillToolbar updates its new controllers itself) or disposed, so no update is lost.

